(BAB 1 Learning as a Daily Practice) Tj
T*
(Learning at work is often treated as a separate activity: a course, a workshop, or a) Tj
T*
(short period of study before returning to real work. That model is convenient, but it) Tj
T*
(separates learning from the conditions in which skills are actually used. Most durable) Tj
T*
(learning happens inside ordinary work, through small experiments, feedback, and) Tj
T*
(reflection on what happened.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A useful starting point is to notice the difference between activity and practice.) Tj
T*
(Activity fills the day with tasks. Practice deliberately improves the ability to perform) Tj
T*
(a task. The difference is attention. A person who answers support tickets for a year may) Tj
T*
(become faster, but a person who reviews a sample of those tickets each week and compares) Tj
T*
(them with a quality standard will improve in a more directed way.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Deliberate practice requires a target that is specific enough to observe. A vague goal) Tj
T*
(such as becoming better at communication is difficult to practice. A specific goal such) Tj
T*
(as explaining a technical decision in five sentences without jargon can be practiced,) Tj
T*
(observed, and improved. Specific goals turn learning from a mood into a sequence of) Tj
T*
(small tests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Feedback is the second condition. Without feedback, practice can reinforce mistakes.) Tj
T*
(Feedback does not need to come from a manager or a formal review. It can come from a) Tj
T*
(customer response, a failed test, a comparison with an example of good work, or a short) Tj
T*
(conversation with a colleague. The important quality is honesty. Feedback that avoids) Tj
T*
(the difficult part teaches very little.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Reflection is the third condition. A short review after a meaningful task can turn) Tj
T*
(experience into knowledge. The review asks what was expected, what happened, and what) Tj
T*
(will change next time. It does not need to be written in a formal report. A few lines in) Tj
T*
(a notebook are enough. The value comes from making the comparison explicit rather than) Tj
T*
(leaving it to memory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(These three conditions are simple, but they are fragile in a busy environment. When) Tj
T*
(deadlines press, practice becomes activity, feedback becomes polite silence, and) Tj
T*
(reflection disappears. A team that wants to learn must protect these conditions) Tj
T*
(deliberately. That protection is a management decision, not a personal virtue.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
endstream
