(BAB 2 Designing Work That Teaches) Tj
T*
(Some work teaches more than other work. A task that is repetitive and fully specified) Tj
T*
(offers little room for growth after the first few repetitions. A task that contains a) Tj
T*
(real problem, a clear standard, and access to feedback offers much more. The design of) Tj
T*
(work therefore shapes the learning that is possible. A manager who wants a capable team) Tj
T*
(must pay attention to how tasks are assigned, not only to who is assigned.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(One useful design principle is to make the standard visible. People learn faster when) Tj
T*
(they can compare their output with a concrete example of good work. The example should) Tj
T*
(come with an explanation of why it is good. Without the explanation, people may copy the) Tj
T*
(surface details and miss the reasoning. With it, they can transfer the principle to a) Tj
T*
(different situation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Another principle is to vary the difficulty on purpose. Work that is always easy becomes) Tj
T*
(boring, while work that is always overwhelming becomes discouraging. A sequence that) Tj
T*
(moves from supported practice to independent practice keeps attention engaged. The) Tj
T*
(support can be a checklist, a pair session, or a review before delivery. The goal is to) Tj
T*
(remove support gradually as competence grows.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Handovers are an underrated learning opportunity. When a task moves from one person to) Tj
T*
(another, the explanation reveals assumptions that were previously invisible. A good) Tj
T*
(handover asks the receiver to restate the goal, the constraints, and the next action. If) Tj
T*
(the receiver cannot restate them, the handover is incomplete. This practice reduces) Tj
T*
(errors and builds shared understanding.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Meetings can also teach or waste time depending on their design. A meeting with no) Tj
T*
(decision, no owner, and no record of what changed produces little learning. A short) Tj
T*
(meeting that reviews evidence, makes a decision, and records the reasoning produces a) Tj
T*
(reusable lesson. The difference is not the length. It is whether the meeting creates) Tj
T*
(knowledge that survives the room.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Finally, work should leave room for a post mortem that is not a search for blame. A post) Tj
T*
(mortem is useful when it explains the conditions that made an error likely and) Tj
T*
(identifies a change that reduces the chance of repetition. When it becomes a trial,) Tj
T*
(people protect themselves instead of explaining what happened. The learning stops, and) Tj
T*
(the same error returns in a new form.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
endstream
