45 800 Td
(A learning culture is often described in terms of attitudes: curiosity, openness,) Tj
T*
(humility. Those attitudes matter, but they are not enough on their own. Culture is also) Tj
T*
(a set of routines that make certain behaviours easier than others. If a team has no time) Tj
T*
(for reflection, no access to feedback, and no place to store what it learned, curiosity) Tj
T*
(has nowhere to go.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The routines do not need to be elaborate. A weekly review of one difficult case can be) Tj
T*
(enough to surface a recurring problem. A shared folder with short notes can be enough to) Tj
T*
(preserve a lesson. A checklist can be enough to prevent a common error. The value comes) Tj
T*
(from repetition and from the willingness to improve the routine when it stops working.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(It is also important to measure learning in a way that reflects reality. The number of) Tj
T*
(training hours completed is a weak measure because it records attendance rather than) Tj
T*
(capability. A better measure is the number of tasks completed with less support, the) Tj
T*
(time taken to resolve a recurring problem, or the reduction in repeated errors. These) Tj
T*
(measures are closer to the work and harder to fake.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Leaders influence these routines by what they reward. If people are rewarded only for) Tj
T*
(speed, reflection will be treated as overhead. If people are rewarded for improving a) Tj
T*
(process without acknowledging the cost of the improvement, the team may optimize one) Tj
T*
(part and damage another. A balanced view of performance makes it possible to learn) Tj
T*
(without hiding the trade-offs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The final point is patience. Learning routines often look inefficient in the short term) Tj
T*
(because their benefits appear later. A team that abandons a routine after two weeks) Tj
T*
(because it did not produce an immediate result will keep returning to the same problems.) Tj
T*
(The routine needs enough time to become normal and enough honesty to be adjusted. That) Tj
T*
(combination is what turns a collection of individuals into a team that can improve.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Learning at work is therefore not a separate project. It is a way of designing tasks,) Tj
T*
(giving feedback, reflecting on results, and preserving what was learned. When those) Tj
T*
(habits are present, experience becomes more than the passage of time. It becomes a) Tj
T*
(resource that the whole team can use.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
endstream
